# Lune Design System v2

When designing, building, or changing UI in the Lune V6 dashboard, treat the
sibling `lds` repository (`../lds/design-system.md` and `../lds/tokens.json`) as
the authority. Do not cite external platform guidelines.

## Required

1. Use generated tokens (`--accent`, `--forest`, `--control-*`, `--text-*`, `--separator`, `--surface-*`, `--fill-forest`, `--bg-glow`). Do not invent parallel palettes or hardcode hex / `0x` colours.
2. Product colour is amber for heat/action and forest for healthy state and selected navigation. Light/dark follows `prefers-color-scheme`.
3. Touch targets: `--control-height` (44px) for primary controls, `--control-compact` (32px) for provision forms, `--nav-item-height` (36px) for sidebar rows, `--nav-row-height` (52px) for the compact tab bar.
4. Contrast: meet WCAG AA. Never convey status with colour alone — pair with label, icon, or shape.
5. Match shared kit classes (`.ui-btn`, `.ui-input`, `.ui-select`, `.ui-row`) and LDS primitives (`dial()`, `luneMark()`, `liveStatusHtml()`, `loopCellHtml()` / `manifoldRowHtml()`, `comfortSliderHtml()`, live|provision split).
6. Compact breakpoint is 900px. Selected destinations use shape plus forest fill.
7. Thermal glow belongs only on the brand mark and halo dial. The only page atmosphere is tokenised `--bg-glow`.
8. Token changes happen in `lds`. This repo only installs via `lds.yaml` and `make design-tokens`.

## Do not

- Nested cards, equally prominent metric-card grids, or decorative glass/gradient chrome
- Network font fetches (including Google Fonts) or Montserrat
- Separate light/dark or accent preferences
- Hover-only help or invisible keyboard focus
